{% extends "_layout.html.j2" %}
{% import "_parts.html.j2" as t %}
{% set c = collections[0] %}
{% block content %}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px">{% if full_name %}Hi {{ full_name.split(' ')[0] }}.{% else %}Hello,{% endif %}</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 14px">Thanks, that is a yes for <code>{{ c.collection }}</code>.</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 14px">One thing has to happen before I can do anything: each person you named
has to visit <a href="https://dc.cyverse.org">dc.cyverse.org</a> and sign in once through CyVerse
SSO. The catalogue has no local passwords and no account exists until first login, so until they
have signed in there is no user for me to add as an administrator.</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 8px">Once they have, reply here and I will:</p>
<ol style="margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px">
<li style="margin:0 0 6px">create the organization
<a href="https://dc.cyverse.org/organization/{{ c.slug }}">dc.cyverse.org/organization/{{ c.slug }}</a>
from your collection metadata;</li>
<li style="margin:0 0 6px">add your people as admins;</li>
<li style="margin:0 0 6px">run the load once, creating {{ c.n_datasets }}
dataset{{ '' if c.n_datasets == 1 else 's' }}, one per folder directly under
<code>{{ c.collection }}</code>;</li>
<li style="margin:0 0 6px">send you the landing pages so you can check every resource link
resolves.</li>
</ol>

<p style="margin:0 0 14px">Reckon on under an hour from your confirmation.</p>

{{ t.handover(c) }}

{%- if c.n_untitled %}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px">Most of what you will want to do first is the dataset descriptions:
{{ c.n_untitled }} of your {{ c.n_datasets }} datasets arrive with a directory name and an empty
description, because the folders carry no metadata of their own.</p>
{%- endif %}

{{ t.signature(sender_name, sender_title) }}
{% endblock %}
